From ebe7dccc8d6f8c8a81753a09c07c55daf9acc867 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 01:46:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(lifecycle-guard): a quoted data-sink pattern's | bash is
 no output sink [daveey]

A hub chat's read-only `grep -E "...|\[bash, ?\"-[lc]|..." local.py ...` was refused with
"the scan depth limit was reached (depth 8)": the quote-blind sink regex read `|\[bash` in the
pattern as a pipe into bash, so every adjacent quote pair was walked as printed shell code. The
escaped `\"` shifted pairing and put local.py in command position (local.py -> ~/.bashrc ->
bash_completion, past depth 8).

iter_printed_shell_payloads now also requires a sink after _mask_data_sink_arguments
(fail-closed: lines piping into a shell and arguments carrying `$(`, backticks, `<(`, `>(`, `\!`
or dot-commands are never masked). shell_sink=True callers are unchanged. Nit 3's `| grep bash`
false-sink rows move to no-sink; real sinks (`grep ... | bash`, `| awk bash`) stay fail-closed.

Self-heal lifecycleguard-f82a8e8dd311 (t_f59ff0fb76b5e065).
